{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KoW1oQVqEdwH2SdrswSdLr","type":"tool_result","content":"[measure] Implement cmd/truncate core file size operations (srd083 R1.1, R1.2, R1.3, R1.4)\nOPEN\n---\ncobbler_generation: generation-run44\ncobbler_index: 0\n---\n\ndeliverable_type: code\n\nrequired_reading:\n  - docs/specs/software-requirements/srd083-truncate.yaml (SRD for truncate -- read requirements R1.1 through R1.4)\n  - pkg/sizeparse/ (size string parsing with unit suffixes -- truncate uses SIZE with K/M/G suffixes)\n  - pkg/sys/sigpipe.go (SIGPIPE handler pattern -- all cmd/ utilities must call InstallSIGPIPEHandler)\n  - cmd/stat/main.go (reference implementation of a similar file-metadata utility in this project)\n\nfiles:\n  - path: cmd/truncate/main.go\n    action: create\n    note: truncate command implementation -- core file truncation with --size flag and argument parsing\n\nrequirements:\n  - id: R1\n    text: Implement srd083 R1.1 -- parse command-line flags and positional arguments per the SRD\n  - id: R2\n    text: Implement srd083 R1.2 -- set file size to the exact value specified by --size\n  - id: R3\n    text: Implement srd083 R1.3 -- create files that do not exist when specified as arguments\n  - id: R4\n    text: Implement srd083 R1.4 -- support --no-create (-c) to suppress file creation for nonexistent files\n\ndesign_decisions:\n  - id: D1\n    text: Call sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() at the start of main per project convention\n  - id: D2\n    text: Use pkg/sizeparse.Parse or ParseWithOptions for --size argument parsing with unit suffixes\n  - id: D3\n    text: Use os.Truncate for setting file size after creating/opening the file\n  - id: D4\n    text: Exit codes and error messages must match GNU truncate behavior per the SRD\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    text: cmd/truncate/main.go compiles with \"go build ./cmd/truncate/\"\n  - id: AC2\n    text: \"go vet ./cmd/truncate/\" passes with no warnings