{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01FKdPkngbUTPYjtRnuaHtN2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting observations:\n1. `-s=100` treats `=100` as the SIZE value, which is invalid. So `-s` consumes the rest of the flag group as the value, NOT using `=` syntax.\n2. `-s100` works, treating `100` as the size (rest of flag group is the value)\n3. `--size 100` works with a space\n4. `-cs100` works (c flag + s100 as size)\n5. `-cs 100` works (c flag + s followed by space and value)\n\nSo for short flag parsing:\n\n\n- `-s` followed by remaining characters in the flag group becomes the value, or if nothing remains, the next argument is used\n- `-c` is a boolean flag that doesn't consume a value\n- `-r` works the same way as `-s`, taking either the rest of the flag group or the next argument as its value\n\nLet me verify how `-r` behaves with these same patterns.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":55238,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708},"output_tokens":28,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a61810ff-70f4-4e3b-8473-0c1f0b2a6146","uuid":"da333429-1832-41de-ae48-218124d76d90"}
